 "own_rule_reading": [
  "k is the GLOBAL bar index of the loaded window (the text writes VWAP with k - session_start + 1, so k and session_start are the same global index); 'k >= 25' is therefore a global warm-up that only touches the window's first session.",
  "session = one ET calendar day of the RTH master (engine day_id); session_start = that day's first bar.",
  "VWAP proxy = plain mean of close[session_start..k] (inclusive), exactly the text's formula; no volume.",
  "ATR20 = mean(high - low) over GLOBAL bars k-19..k inclusive (may reach back into the prior session early in a day); plain range, not true range, as written.",
  "signal on bar k's close, strict inequalities (> VWAP + 2.5*ATR20 -> short, < VWAP - 2.5*ATR20 -> long); entry at bar k+1's open; bar k+1 must be in the SAME session (a signal on the session's last bar is not taken - the text also says flat at the session's last bar).",
  "stop and target distances use ATR20 of the signal bar k, fixed for the trade, measured from the ENTRY price (k+1's open).",
  "intrabar checks start ON the entry bar k+1 (its high/low after the open); on every later bar a gap through a level books that bar's open (stop gap or target gap); if stop and target are both touched inside one bar the STOP wins (the text gives no order; stop-first is the conservative reading).",
  "flat at the session's last bar = exit at that bar's CLOSE if neither level was hit (levels are still checked intrabar on the last bar first).",
  "one trade per session: the first bar k whose close crosses a band is the only entry of that day; after the exit nothing re-enters that day; signals while in the trade are ignored.",
  "1 contract, no ML, no other filter; the window and master are the prereg's (2010-06-07..2016-06-30, NOADJ_NQ_5m_RTH.csv)."
 ],
